      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Route 419 cuts through the heart of town as Main Street, linking it to Womelsdorf and Schaefferstown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newmanstown%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mill Creek skirts the west side of Newmanstown, flowing north into Tulpehocken Creek and eventually the Schuylkill River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newmanstown%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town is bordered to the northeast by Marion Township and Heidelberg Township in neighboring Berks County.",
